 **Edge cases and pitfalls:**
-*   If all weights are zero (no Gaussians intersect the ray), the sums are zero, resulting in a loss of 0. This is generally acceptable as there is no depth to constrain.
-*   Numerical precision: If the depth distribution is very narrow, $\mathcal{D}_{sq} \approx \mathcal{D}^2$, leading to potential cancellation errors. However, in standard 3DGS optimization, this is rarely an issue due to the nature of the opacity accumulation.
