 ## Background
-The Depth Distribution Constraint was introduced in the context of 3D Gaussian Splatting optimization to address the issue of "floaters" and poor structural reconstruction. It was notably used in the LE3D method to enhance structural details for downstream tasks like refocusing [S1]. The formulation as a variance minimization ($\mathcal{D}_{sq} - \mathcal{D}^2$) is derived from the statistical definition of variance, treating the depth distribution as a probability distribution weighted by Gaussian contributions [S2].
